WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.132 --> 00:00:08.144
Once upon a time, there was a man who had three sons named Peter, Paul, and Boots.

2
00:00:08.145 --> 00:00:13.724
The father was very poor. He didn't have a single penny to give to his sons.

3
00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:21.265
One day he said to his sons, "I am poor. I have nothing to give you.

4
00:00:21.266 --> 00:00:27.502
It is time for you to lead your own lives in the world."

5
00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:33.721
As the brothers were preparing to start their new lives, a man came to their town.

6
00:00:33.722 --> 00:00:39.424
He said to everyone, "Our great king has two terrible tasks.

7
00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:44.656
First, you must chop down a giant oak tree that is blocking his window.

8
00:00:44.657 --> 00:00:56.207
Next, you must dig him a well. If you complete these two tasks, he will give you half of his kingdom and half of his treasure.

9
00:00:56.208 --> 00:01:01.650
If you fail these tasks, you will be sent to a faraway island."

10
00:01:01.651 --> 00:01:06.902
The father was delighted. The tasks did not seem too hard.

11
00:01:06.903 --> 00:01:13.928
The brothers were delighted because they had already chopped down many trees and dug a well for their father.

12
00:01:13.929 --> 00:01:18.628
They set off for the palace with dreams of gold and jewels.

13
00:01:18.629 --> 00:01:27.969
What the king's messenger had not said was that as soon as one chip of the oak's trunk flew off, two more grew back in its place.

14
00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:37.571
The king's messenger also forgot to say that the king's palace was on top of a high hill, and that this hill was made of solid rock.

15
00:01:37.572 --> 00:01:44.386
When the brothers entered the forest, they heard something chopping and hacking away among the trees.

16
00:01:44.387 --> 00:01:47.525
"Do you hear that sound?" asked Boots.

17
00:01:47.526 --> 00:01:51.077
"Yes," said Peter and Paul together.

18
00:01:51.078 --> 00:01:56.143
"Is it unusual for a woodcutter to chop trees?" asked Paul.

19
00:01:56.144 --> 00:02:04.678
"No, but this sounds strange," said Boots. "I want to see what it is."

20
00:02:04.679 --> 00:02:08.294
"Oh, Boots! You're the one who is strange.

21
00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:17.687
Our father was too poor to give you a real name, so he named you after an old pair of boots." His brothers laughed.

22
00:02:17.688 --> 00:02:20.239
Boots didn't care what they said.

23
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:26.014
He walked towards the noise, and when he reached where it was coming from, he couldn't believe what he saw.

24
00:02:26.015 --> 00:02:32.564
There hung an ax, hacking and chopping all by itself.

25
00:02:32.565 --> 00:02:37.616
"Good day!" said Boots. "You look busy. Can I help you?"

26
00:02:37.617 --> 00:02:42.419
"Yes, I am busy. And, yes, you can help.

27
00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:49.931
I've stood here chopping and hacking for a long time waiting for you," said the ax.

28
00:02:49.932 --> 00:02:54.331
"Well, I'm here, and you can come with us," said Boots.

29
00:02:54.332 --> 00:03:00.539
He took the ax and tucked it under his belt.

30
00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.060
From the forest the brothers walked into the mountains.

31
00:03:04.061 --> 00:03:10.639
The mountains were very rocky, but soon they heard a noise that sounded like digging.

32
00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:19.023
"I wonder," said Boots, "what could be digging and shoveling in all this rock?"

33
00:03:19.024 --> 00:03:25.460
"There you go acting strange again. Poor Boots." Peter laughed.

34
00:03:25.461 --> 00:03:28.919
"It's just a woodpecker," continued Paul.

35
00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:34.600
"This sounds different," said Boots. "I think I'll go see what it is."

36
00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:40.362
He climbed up the rocks. His brothers laughed and made fun of him.

37
00:03:40.363 --> 00:03:43.618
But he didn't let their teasing upset him.

38
00:03:43.619 --> 00:03:47.856
When he got to the top, he couldn't believe what he saw.

39
00:03:47.857 --> 00:03:52.170
There was a shovel that stood digging all by itself.

40
00:03:52.171 --> 00:03:57.121
"Good day!" said Boots. "You look busy. Can I help you?"

41
00:03:57.122 --> 00:04:03.988
"Yes, I am busy," said the shovel, "and yes, you can help.

42
00:04:03.989 --> 00:04:12.310
I've stood here digging and shoveling for a long time waiting for you."

43
00:04:12.311 --> 00:04:17.191
"Well, I'm here, and you can come with us," said Boots.

44
00:04:17.192 --> 00:04:20.775
He took the shovel and put it over his shoulder.

45
00:04:20.776 --> 00:04:27.050
After climbing over the mountains, the brothers were thirsty, so they stopped at a brook.

46
00:04:27.051 --> 00:04:31.983
"I wonder where all this water comes from," said Boots.

47
00:04:31.984 --> 00:04:38.052
"We wonder if you're sick in the head." Peter and Paul laughed.

48
00:04:38.053 --> 00:04:42.629
"Still I would like to see it for myself," said Boots.

49
00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:47.805
"You're crazy, or you'll go crazy soon," said Paul.

50
00:04:47.806 --> 00:04:53.978
"The brook's here; that's all that matters. Who cares where it comes from?"

51
00:04:53.979 --> 00:05:01.245
"Still I'd like to see it just the same," said Boots. So he went away.

52
00:05:01.246 --> 00:05:07.240
He followed the brook and soon he could no longer hear the laughter of his brothers.

53
00:05:07.241 --> 00:05:14.090
The brook got smaller and smaller, and finally he couldn't believe what he saw.

54
00:05:14.091 --> 00:05:19.449
There was a large walnut, and out of that walnut came a stream of water.

55
00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:24.857
"Good day!" said Boots. "You look busy. Can I help?"

56
00:05:24.858 --> 00:05:36.100
"Yes, I am," said the walnut. "And yes, you can, because I have let this water run for a long time waiting for you."

57
00:05:36.101 --> 00:05:44.260
"Well, I'm here," said Boots. He plugged the hole with some moss, so the water wouldn't run out anymore.

58
00:05:44.261 --> 00:05:47.571
Then he stuffed the walnut into his pocket.

59
00:05:47.572 --> 00:05:50.482
His brothers hadn't waited for him.

60
00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:59.108
They decided that they didn't want to share the kingdom and the treasure with their strange brother, Boots.

61
00:05:59.109 --> 00:06:08.624
The oak was now twice as wide and twice as tall as it had been at first because two chips grew for every one chopped out.

62
00:06:08.625 --> 00:06:14.949
When Boots reached the city, his two brothers had already tried and failed.

63
00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:19.601
The king was very angry; he had seen many men try and fail.

64
00:06:19.602 --> 00:06:28.721
He looked at Boots and said, "If you are going to perform as well as your brothers, then go directly to the ship.

65
00:06:28.722 --> 00:06:32.003
I don't want to watch another person fail."

66
00:06:32.004 --> 00:06:36.771
"Well, I can't succeed unless I try," said Boots.

67
00:06:36.772 --> 00:06:42.572
The king wasn't happy, but he gave Boots permission, and Boots took out his ax.

68
00:06:42.573 --> 00:06:47.243
"Chop away!" he said to the ax, and away it chopped.

69
00:06:47.244 --> 00:06:56.666
It chopped out four chips for every two that grew back, so it wasn't long before the old oak came down.

70
00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:59.599
When that was done, Boots took out his shovel.

71
00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:06.993
"Dig away!" he said to the shovel. And the shovel began to dig and dig.

72
00:07:06.994 --> 00:07:10.009
The rocks flew like leaves in the wind.

73
00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:13.998
Soon he had dug the well, but still there was no water.

74
00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:20.565
Boots took out the walnut, he placed it in one corner of the well, and then he pulled out the moss.

75
00:07:20.566 --> 00:07:26.736
"Run away!" said Boots. And so the water ran out.

76
00:07:26.737 --> 00:07:33.109
At first the well filled with water very slowly, but soon the well filled and made a stream.

77
00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:36.815
The king had all the water he could ever want.

78
00:07:36.816 --> 00:07:44.127
The king gave Boots half his kingdom and half his treasure as promised, but he was so pleased with Boots, he said,

79
00:07:44.128 --> 00:07:47.998
"Is there anything else that I can give you?"

80
00:07:47.999 --> 00:07:57.057
Boots thought for a second and said, "Well, it would be nice if you'd let all the people who failed come back from the island."

81
00:07:57.058 --> 00:08:02.787
The king agreed and said, "Still that is a gift to those who failed.

82
00:08:02.788 --> 00:08:06.720
Is there anything else I can give to you?"

83
00:08:06.721 --> 00:08:17.872
Boots remembered that his brothers made fun of his name, and he said, "Yes, I would like to change my name. Can I be called Mr. Boots?"

84
00:08:17.873 --> 00:08:30.032
The king smiled and said, "Yes, Mr. Boots, you can."

